Inspection Endpoints
Create Inspection
Creates a new equipment inspection with items and optional images.
Endpoint: POST /inspections
Authorization: Required
Request Headers:
httpAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
IdempotencyKey: <unique_request_id>
Content-Type: multipart/form-data
```

**Request Body (multipart/form-data):**
```
data: {
  "equipmentId": "uuid",
  "generalNotes": "General inspection notes",
  "overallCondition": "S",
  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Engine",
      "subCategory": "Oil Level",
      "condition": "S",
      "notes": "Oil level is optimal",
      "recommendation": "Continue regular checks"
    },
    {
      "category": "Tires",
      "subCategory": "Front Left",
      "condition": "B",
      "notes": "Tire showing wear",
      "recommendation": "Replace within 30 days"
    }
  ]
}

// Optional image files
item_0_images: [File, File] // Up to 5 images for item at index 0
item_1_images: [File, File] // Up to 5 images for item at index 1
inspectionImages: [File, File] // Up to 5 general inspection images
Field Definitions:

equipmentId (string, required): UUID of equipment being inspected
generalNotes (string, optional): Overall inspection notes
overallCondition (enum, required): Overall condition rating

Values: "S" (Serviceable), "O" (Operational), "A" (Awaiting Parts), "B" (Beyond Repair), "C" (Condemned)


items (array, required): Array of inspection items (minimum 1)

category (string, required): Item category
subCategory (string, required): Item subcategory
condition (enum, required): Item condition (S/O/A/B/C)
notes (string, optional): Item-specific notes
recommendation (string, optional): Recommended action



Image Upload:

Field naming: item_{index}_images where index matches the item array position
Maximum 5 images per item
Supported formats: JPEG, PNG, PDF
Maximum file size: 10MB per file

Response: 201 Created
json{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Inspection created successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": "uuid",
    "equipmentId": "uuid",
    "datePerformed": "2025-11-25T12:00:00Z"
  }
}
Idempotency:
If the same IdempotencyKey is sent again for the same equipment, the API returns:
200 OK
json{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Inspection created successfully "
}
Error Responses:
400 Bad Request
json{
  "success": false,
  "message": "IdempotencyKey header is required"
}
json{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Equipment not found!"
}
json{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Invalid JSON data in request body"
}
401 Unauthorized
json{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Authentication required"
}

Get Inspections by Equipment ID
Retrieves all inspections for a specific equipment with pagination and filtering.
Endpoint: GET /inspections/equipment/:id
Authorization: Required
Request Headers:
httpAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
Path Parameters:

id (string, required): Equipment UUID

Query Parameters:

page (integer, optional, default: 1): Page number
limit (integer, optional, default: 10): Items per page (max: 100)
sortBy (string, optional, default: "createdAt"): Sort field
sortOrder (string, optional, default: "desc"): Sort order ("asc" or "desc")
condition (string, optional): Filter by condition ("S" or "B")
startDate (ISO date, optional): Filter inspections from this date
endDate (ISO date, optional): Filter inspections to this date

Example Request:
httpGET /inspections/equipment/abc-123-def?page=1&limit=10&condition=S&startDate=2025-01-01&endDate=2025-12-31
