Get All Inspections
Retrieves all inspections across all equipment with pagination and filtering.
Endpoint: GET /inspections
Authorization: Required
Request Headers:
httpAuthorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
Query Parameters:
Same as "Get Inspections by Equipment ID" (except no equipment filter)
Response: Same structure as "Get Inspections by Equipment ID"

Data Models
Condition Enum
typescriptenum Status {
  S = "Serviceable"        // Fully operational
  O = "Operational"        // Functional with minor issues
  A = "Awaiting Parts"     // Non-functional, awaiting repair
  B = "Beyond Repair"      // Cannot be economically repaired
  C = "Condemned"          // Permanently removed from service
}
User Roles
typescriptenum UserRole {
  PLATADMIN = "Platform Administrator"
  ADMIN = "Administrator"
  MANAGER = "Manager"
  AUDITOR = "Auditor"
  OFFICER = "Officer"
}

Notes

Idempotency: The IdempotencyKey header is required for inspection creation to prevent duplicate submissions. Use a unique identifier (UUID recommended) for each request.
File Uploads: When uploading inspection images, ensure field names match the pattern item_{index}_images where the index corresponds to the item's position in the items array.
Pagination: All list endpoints support pagination. The default limit is 10 items per page with a maximum of 100.
Date Filtering: Use ISO 8601 format for date parameters (e.g., 2025-11-25T12:00:00Z).
Null Fields: The API automatically removes null fields from inspection items in responses for cleaner data.
Access Control:

Dashboard stats: ADMIN, MANAGER, AUDITOR
Inspections: All authenticated users